WEBVTT

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.180
Good-bye!

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.260
Hello, I’m Midorikawa Retasu.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.770
Recently, many people have told me that,

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>“You’re different than before...”</i>

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.860
<i>“You seem to smile more often now.”</i>

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:52.290
For sure, one reason is that I got to know Ichigo-san and the other Mew Mew members.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.790
But, there’s another reason...

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.250
I mean there’s someone in my school I’m kind of interested in.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.970
I’m wondering... if this is love...?

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.110
Well, shall we go together?

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.650
Oh, thank you!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.000
I couldn’t speak to him at that time.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.920
Honestly, I didn’t expect
to see him again.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.380
But a few days later, I saw him in an unexpected place.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.030
There he is again!

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:14.650
Since then, I’ve been making time
to frequently visit the library.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:21.620
I’ve realized that he’s always there...

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.080
He’s always reading at the same spot.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.660
Some of the books seem difficult, some don’t...

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.220
He’s reading day after day.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.290
And, one day –

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.020
Here!

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:44.810
Eh?

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.480
That’s the book you wanted, isn’t it?

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.440
Lamaze Is Not Difficult

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.650
<i>It was actually the next book...</i>

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.610
Thank you very much!

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.330
So, you really like books...

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.240
Eh?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.330
I’ve often seen you around recently.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:11.580
Nowadays girls seldom come to the library to read.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.290
That’s why I took a little interest in you.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.010
R-Really?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.680
What kinds of books do you like?

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.480
Eh?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.390
You know, there’re many kinds of books...

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:28.350
...like, philosophical, how-to, muckraking, or historical books.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:31.810
I read novels... like most people...

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.650
Though my favorite is a foreign photo collection.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:36.820
Photo collection?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.870
Yes.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:45.830
I feel kind of relaxed, looking at towns
or seashores I’ve never been to.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.370
Hmm...

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.450
Am I weird?

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.510
No, not at all.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.290
You are a poet...

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.250
I’m Edomurasaki Norihiro. And you are?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.010
Midorikawa Retasu.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.340
Nice to meet you.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.930
Nice to meet you too.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.470
Ahem~!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.690
And I’m going to the library again today.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.620
What’s up? You look so happy.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.130
No, nothing at all.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.580
Did something nice happen?

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.180
No, not really...

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.560
Perhaps you’ve found a boyfriend!

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:51.140
N-Nope, that’s not it...
I-I mean, umm...

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.640
So you HAVE!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.440
U-Umm, I mean,

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.610
...it’s not that he’s my boyfriend...

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.570
So it’s true!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.320
Retasu found a boyf...

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.780
Ichigo-san! PLEASE!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.660
W-What?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.460
Between you-and-me!

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.100
Between you-and-me!

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.080
Between you-and-me!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.540
Hahahaa~!!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.540
Hahahaa~!!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.130
You guys, guess what? Retasu found a NEW BOYFRIEND!

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.720
Hey! I said between you and me!!

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.670
EHHhh~!??

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.690
Hmm, Retasu found a boyfriend...

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.680
Are you madly in love with each other?

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:36.030
Well, I wonder what kind of boy he is...

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.410
Let see...

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.120
Is he tall?

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.290
No, he isn’t.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.380
Is he an athlete?

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.710
No, he isn’t.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.100
You two are madly in love with each other!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.050
No, we aren’t, Bu-Ling-san.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.260
Isn’t he just playing with you?

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.510
No...

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.850
Is he younger than you, maybe?

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.580
No, he isn’t!

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.710
What’s your boyfriend like?

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:07.020
Well, he is tall,
and he likes reading, and...

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.180
N-Nope! I said he’s not
my boyfriend!!

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.900
So, did he declare his love for you?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.940
Or did you take the initiative?

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:15.780
Hey!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.450
Hey!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.610
I said he’s not my boyfriend~!!!

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.830
Oh, I see.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.330
So you two aren’t lovers...

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.570
That’s what I’ve been saying!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.370
And?

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:31.920
Eh?

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.050
Do you love him, Retasu?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.680
You do!

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.270
What are you doing, Pie?

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.130
I’m gathering data on humans.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.110
Do you have to?

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.720
Humans on Earth are all worthless, you know!

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.740
According to data I’ve already gathered...

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.780
...Man’s ability varies radically from individual to individual.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:06.690
Their body and brain seem to be two
modules functioning independently.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.210
I don’t really know what you mean,

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.660
but in short, humans are imperfect, right?

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.620
I’ll go to gather more data.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.910
Midorikawa-san...

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.080
So...

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.040
Something wrong?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.700
N-Nope... nothing.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.590
I’m sorry.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.550
Eh? I can have it?

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:30.960
Yeah.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.010
Would you please accept it?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.770
C-Certainly... with pleasure!

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.240
I found it in a bookstore I sometimes go to.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:55.870
I bought it, but while reading it, I realized
that this book would suit you better.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.870
But... can I really have this?

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.710
A token of my gratitude.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:02.640
Eh?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.920
I was nothing but a bookworm... but
you had me find something new.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.380
So... I’d like you to accept it.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:13.720
I will.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.270
Thank you very much.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.100
If I could smile like you...

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:24.900
Eh?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:29.900
I mean, I wish I could smile like you...

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.610
You are smiling so nicely now.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.660
You can too, Edomurasaki-san!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:45.830
I used to only have bitter or sad thoughts too.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:54.380
But now I can think positively,
just like that.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:02.180
Because people around me are encouraging... I think that’s my reason.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:06.600
So... I’m sure you can too, Edomurasaki-san.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.020
You think so?

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.070
Yes!

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.380
Let-tu-ce!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.260
Yes?

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.460
Something happened, didn’t it?

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.260
Hmm, that’s a present!

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.970
Oh, there’s no longer any doubt!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.060
Eh? What do you mean?

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:41.530
What do I mean!? As if you didn’t know!

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.930
Eh? Umm... what?

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.570
You don’t realize?

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:50.450
Just imagine. You wouldn’t give a present
to someone you didn’t like, right?

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.900
Retasu and he will be madly in love!

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:55.380
Yup, yup.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.580
Now you’re supposed to –

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.080
Take the plunge!!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.910
Hey, declare your love!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.400
Declare Your Love!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.550
W... w-why do you conclude that?

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.640
Because...

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.400
...you love him, don’t you?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.470
Hehehee...

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:23.180
Well, it’s up to you Retasu.
We won’t say anything more but...

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.360
we’re behind you all the way.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.180
Good luck!

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.310
Well, it’s surprising, isn’t it?

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.130
Is it?

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:38.270
In my opinion, it’s more suriprising that YOU have a boyfriend.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.750
Aoyama-kun is not my...

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.010
He isn’t?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:48.840
That has nothing to do with someone
who’s never had a boyfriend!

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:49.750
You know I...

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:55.440
I’m so happy just to be with you, Zakuro-sama!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.720
But it’d be nice... if you traveled with your
boyfriend to a place like in that photo.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.530
Aoyama-kun...

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.150
Ichigo...

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.760
Err, huh. Hahahaaaa~!

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.200
Oh yeah. Let’s have dinner now!

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.370
Yup!

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.830
U-ugh!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.470
S-Shall we... eat this?

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:31.450
Yeah, it’s delicious!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.250
Ugh, I don’t want to.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.080
Well, but if he eats it...

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.260
“If you eat it, I will too!”

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:39.260
Dream as much as you like!

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.390
Hey Retasu! You haven’t been very sociable with us lately.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.320
Aren’t we good friends?

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:58.450
And we’re going to an interesting place, but we need money.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:11:59.360
Well...

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:00.740
Hrpm!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.740
I am busy today!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.290
Eh?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:07.590
You mean you can’t join us?!

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:09.920
Right, I can’t join you today.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.040
Excuse me, but I’ve to go now!

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:34.710
I’m thinking so positively now; though,
I’m not sure when that changed...

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:39.340
I can remember the happy and sad
times shared with my friends...

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.580
how I got to know them, and the good times together...

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.220
And about Edomurasaki-san...

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.510
Perhaps I’ve known this long ago,
but I can say it clearly now:

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:54.790
I love him.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.750
It’ll be Sunday tomorrow.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:59.710
I know!

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.530
I’m going!

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:43.720
Edomurasaki-san...

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.740
Well, he’s late today...

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.570
Oh, you’re going home early?

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.070
Midorikawa-san...?

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.960
What’s the sudden panic?

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.060
I’m sorry.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.900
What’s the matter?

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:11.510
I...I’ve been thinking of you.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.430
WATER FLEAS!!!

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.620
What?!

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.660
Chimera Anima?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.480
How come?

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.400
This is a database for humans.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.790
Almost all is recorded in analog forms.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:33.370
All right.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:37.330
I can gather basic data here,
though it will be time-consuming.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.720
Go!

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.600
This way!

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.780
They’re eating books!

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:55.610
Let’s get out of here!

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:56.450
Yes!

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:01.810
Satsuki? ...Satsuki!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.150
Satsuki?

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.330
Go ahead without me.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.000
But...

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.630
Thanks to you, I’ve changed.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.820
I’m not what I was, because you encouraged me.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:16.750
Thank you.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:17.700
Oh, wait!

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.810
Satsuki! Satsuki!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:25.750
Edomurasaki-san!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.480
Edomurasaki...

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:30.270
Satsuki?

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:31.130
Satsuki!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.260
Are you okdy, Satsuki?

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:35.720
Norihiro-san...

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.270
Reborn Mint Echo!

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.730
Aaah! We’ve lost!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.950
Hurry! This way!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.090
You too must escape now.

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:59.600
I’m alright. Take care of Satsuki-san!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.000
Wait a moment!

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:10.170
How dare you interrupt Retasu, when
she was going to declare her love?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.300
We’ll never forgive you.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:15.430
Today’s Chimera Animas are so funny.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:22.140
For the Earth’s future,
I’ll be of service ~Nya!

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.100
You guys...

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:33.040
People often say “if’s” in history.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:36.070
I dare say: if the two, who later played the important role in history,

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:39.670
had not happened to be there at that time...

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:44.510
...then the war situation at the end of Edo Period would have been much aggravated,

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:48.640
and the urban areas around Edo Castle would have turned into sea of flame.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:48.640
What’s this?

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.680
Now, we will analyze this problem with dialectic, that is,

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:58.240
the process in which a thesis is sublated by its antithesis to make the synthesis,

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.270
I’m getting sleepy...

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.440
Unbearable...

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:58.240
This reading has a hypnotic effect.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.440
or the higher conclusion.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.870
Fuu-hyou-sen!

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.770
Wuaahh~!

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:07.690
Ouch...

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:12.290
Mew Mew Lettuce METAMORPHO-SE!

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:39.610
Reborn... Lettuce RUSH!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.690
Mew Strawberry, now!

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.840
StrawberBell!!

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:08.370
Well, I’ve gathered the data we need for now.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:13.750
Reborn... Strawberry SURPRISE!!

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:24.400
You did it, Mew Lettuce!

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:28.650
You didn’t get sleepy because you like reading!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:29.600
Excellent!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:33.560
Yeah, I’ve been encouraged after all.

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:55.670
Retasu...

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.760
Don’t worry! I’m alright.

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:07.720
After all, my first love came
to a sad ending.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:11.040
My heart still feels a little pain...

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:15.240
...but someday, before long...

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.690
I’ll be thinking in this way.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.380
I was glad to fall in love.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.460
Summer! Summer vacation!

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:28.340
“Summer vacation” means “falling in love”!

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:32.760
“Falling in love” means
“with Aoyama-kun,” tee-hee *^_^*

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.930
Don’t forget about the Aliens!

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:38.220
PLEASE! Don’t say that when I’m dreaming
such a happy dream!

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.430
What do you think I am, Shirogane?!

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:44.230
Don’t forget I’m a delicate little girl.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:47.650
Next: “The Knight in Blue: I Will Protect You”

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:51.070
What’s that? “I will protect you”? Sounds romantic!

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:54.070
Will you repeat it again please?
